{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "By default, if you register an extension in the playbook file, Antora will enable it automatically. One way to enable an extension only upon request is to specify it using the CLI option ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "--extension"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). However, that alone doesn’t allow you to provide configuration keys or influence the require order. That’s where extension enablement comes into play."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can register an extension in the playbook file, along with optional configuration, then tell Antora not to enable it. You can then use the CLI option ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "--extension"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") to enable it, and it will be registered relative to other extensions enabled through this mechanism. (See "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Load order"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "#load-order"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to understand how extensions are ordered when the CLI is used)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To prevent Antora from enabling an extension specified in the playbook file, set the predefined configuration key "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "enabled"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to the value "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "false"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". When Antora sees that the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "enabled"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key has a value of "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "false"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", it will not register the extension."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "antora:\n  extensions:\n  - require: ./my-extension.js\n    enabled: false\n    custom: value"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yaml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "An extension that is not enabled"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "enabled"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key to quickly turn off an extension without having to remove it from the playbook. More likely, though, you configure it this way so it can be enabled using the CLI option. In order to do so, you need a way to reference it, which is the purpose of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "id"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "id"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key specifies an ID you can reference using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "--extension"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " CLI option to enable an extension that’s marked as not enabled in the playbook file. When the value of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "--extension"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " CLI option matches the value of this key, that extension is enabled (rather than appending the extension to the list of extensions). If you don’t specify an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "id"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", the value of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "require"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key serves as the extension’s ID."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "First, let’s give our extension an ID:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "antora:\n  extensions:\n  - id: my-extension\n    require: ./my-extension.js\n    enabled: false\n    custom: value"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yaml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "An extension with an ID that is not enabled"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Now we can now enable this extension from the CLI as follows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "literal",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "$ antora --extension my-extension antora-playbook.yml"
              }
            ],
            "language": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Whereas normally the value of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "--extension"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " CLI option is a require request, in the case when you are enabling an extension, the value is the ID of the extension entry in the playbook file."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you don’t assign an ID to the extension entry, you can reference the value of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "require"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key instead."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "literal",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "$ antora --extension ./my-extension.js antora-playbook.yml"
              }
            ],
            "language": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In this case, Antora looks for the first entry in the list of extensions whose "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "require"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key matches the value of the CLI option."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If Antora can’t locate an entry that matches the value of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "--extension"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " CLI option, it falls back to treating the value as a require request."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "By default, declaring and enabling an extension in the playbook also determines its load order. Any enabled extensions declared in the playbook are loaded first in playbook order, followed by any extensions enabled through the CLI."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "However, the CLI still has an opportunity to influence this load order. By default, if the value of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "--extension"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " option matches an extension declared in the playbook (id or require value), the load order of the extension is updated. That extension acts as though it’s not declared in the playbook and enabled by the CLI instead. Yet, the configuration from the playbook is still used."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Let’s consider an example:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "antora:\n  extensions:\n  - require: ./from-playbook.js\n    custom: value"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yaml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "An extension declared in the playbook"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Now, if we want to load an extension before this extension, we can do so using the CLI:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "literal",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "$ antora --extension ./from-cli.js --extension ./from-playbook.js antora-playbook.yml"
              }
            ],
            "language": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The from-cli.js extension will be loaded first, followed by the from-playbook.js extension. Had we not referenced the from-playbook.js extension using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "--extension"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " option, it would have been loaded first."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "This technique also works for an extension declared in the playbook as not enabled (i.e., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "enabled: false"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ")."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To turn off this reordering and retain the order of the extension as listed in the playbook, you can set the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "order"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key to the value "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "fixed"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". (The default value is "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "auto"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ")."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "antora:\n  extensions:\n  - require: ./from-playbook.js\n    order: fixed\n    enabled: false\n    custom: value"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yaml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "An extension declared in the playbook with a fixed order"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Now, the load order is not updated when the extension is enabled using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "--extension"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " CLI option."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "load-order",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Load order"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Enable an Extension"
      }
    ]
  }
}
